-- title:
--   Rigidity of ± P level structures for M ≥ 4
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ ($p$ prime), let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $4 \le M$ and with $M \ne 0$ in $K$, and let $E_0$ be a Weierstrass curve over $K$ that is elliptic. Let $s$ be a subset of the affine point group $E_0(K)$ subject to the condition that there is a point $P$ of exact additive order $M$ with $s$ equal to the set of all $T$ of the form $T = (u : \mathrm{ZMod}\ M).\mathrm{val} \cdot P$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathrm{ZMod}\ M$ lying in the subgroup generated by the trivial subgroup together with the powers of $-1$; that is, $s = \{P, -P\}$, described via multiplication of $P$ by the natural-number representatives of $\pm 1 \bmod M$. The assertion is that the set of those $\gamma$ in the stabiliser of $E_0$ for the action of the group $\mathrm{VariableChange}\ K$ of admissible changes of variable (so $\gamma \bullet E_0 = E_0$) with the property that for every $T \in s$ there is $T' \in s$ with $\mathrm{Point.vcInvFun}\ \gamma\ E_0$ applied to $T$ heterogeneously equal to $T'$, is finite of cardinality exactly $2$. Here $\mathrm{vcInvFun}$ for a change of variable $C = (u; r, s, t)$ sends $0$ to $0$ and an affine point $(x,y)$ to the point $(u^{-2}(x-r),\ u^{-3}(y-t-s(x-r)))$ of $C \bullet E_0$, and heterogeneous equality is used because that target type is not syntactically the point type of $E_0$.
--
--   This is the rigidity of $\Gamma_1(M)$-level structures taken up to sign for $M \ge 4$: only the identity and the negation $(-1; 0, -a_1, -a_3)$ preserve the pair $\{P,-P\}$ attached to a point of exact order $M$ (the statement fails for $M = 3$ on $j = 0$ and for $M = 2$ on $j = 1728$). It feeds the count of variable-change orbits of such level structures in [`WeierstrassCurve.natCard_torsionOrbit_bot_variableChange_eq_jWidthChar`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.natCard_torsionOrbit_bot_variableChange_eq_jWidthChar).
-- source:
